  "description": "The Intl algorithms shared by the Broiler JavaScript engines (ECMA-402), over the locale data an engine hands in: the data contract (the generated tables as an IIntlDataSet, decoded once into the question-level ILocaleData, with CompositeLocaleData ordering the shared data, an optional secondary provider, and the locale's parent and root), the statuses that replace engine errors, locale identifiers, negotiation, Intl.Locale's record, Locale info and supportedValuesOf, the Intl mathematical value, the digit options, FormatNumericToString, plural rules and ranges, number formatting with list, relative-time and display-name formatting, date-time formatting with ranges, day periods, hour cycles and zone names over CLDR's metazone history and Intl over Temporal, and duration formatting.",
